# vim1s-desktop :: per-user session overrides
# Copy to ~/.config/vim1s/session.env and uncomment what you need. Sourced by vim1s-session
# (before the compositor starts) for BOTH Hyprland and sway. Every variable is exported.
#
# Only names verified in source are listed:
#   AQ_*        aquamarine v0.15.1 docs/env.md  (Hyprland's backend library)
#   HYPRLAND_*  Hyprland v0.56.2 src/render/OpenGL.cpp
#   WLR_RENDERER, EGL_LOG_LEVEL, MESA_GLES_VERSION_OVERRIDE are long-standing documented
#   wlroots/Mesa variables, but NOT re-checked against wlroots 0.20 / Mesa 26.2.2 here
#   (their upstream GitLab was unreachable from the build environment).
#   Panfrost-specific PAN_MESA_DEBUG values: check docs/envvars.rst of YOUR Mesa (26.2.2)
#   before using one; they were not verifiable from this build environment.

# --- which DRM card drives the display (Hyprland) --------------------------------------
# aquamarine only accepts KMS-capable cards, so Panfrost's render-only node is skipped
# automatically. Pin explicitly if probe order ever confuses it (first = primary):
#AQ_DRM_DEVICES=/dev/dri/card1

# --- if the new S4 KMS driver misbehaves (Hyprland) --------------------------------------
#AQ_NO_ATOMIC=1                # fall back to legacy (non-atomic) modesetting
#AQ_NO_MODIFIERS=1             # allocate scanout buffers without format modifiers
#HYPRLAND_EGL_NO_MODIFIERS=1   # renderer side: import dmabufs as LINEAR only
#AQ_TRACE=1                    # very verbose backend log (goes to the session log)

# --- Mesa ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#EGL_LOG_LEVEL=debug           # why EGL picked/failed a platform or driver
#MESA_GLES_VERSION_OVERRIDE=3.0

# --- sway / wlroots -------------------------------------------------------------------------
#WLR_RENDERER=pixman           # CPU rendering: proves KMS works even if Panfrost/Mesa does not
